From 5b859e07883bfff4c84326566d38ca32b180e7b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: q56-scratch <q56@scratch>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:47:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] substrate: maspsx models cc1psx -G8's .sdata choice for small
 initialized objects (owner ruling Q68, step 13)

Owner rulings Q65/Q68 (amendment A3): under maspsx -G<n> an initialized object of <= n bytes that our cc1 put
in `.data` moves to `.sdata` as a unit (its .globl/.align/.type/.size head, label and data), as cc1psx -G8
emits it. Calibration: docs/grind/gp-model-2026-09-30.md A.3 (global objects) and A.3b, added here
(initialized statics, 3-byte arrays at +0/+4, an 8-byte .string array; cc1psx_static_probe.sh). Layer-2 round 2
also calibrated function-scope initialized statics (cc1 names like fl.4 / fc.5): cc1psx -G8 puts them in .sdata
in source order and ours matches (none exist in the tree). Sizes come from .size; .string/.asciz count the
decoded bytes + 1, .ascii escape-aware. Tests: tools/maspsx/tests/test_small_data_sdata.py (our cc1's real
output for the probe, cc1psx's sections as expectations), engine test. Inert without -G (byte-neutral here).
